Build C++17 <filesystem>, a minimal std::pmr, and __libcpp_verbose_abort into libc++.1.dylib.

Darling's LLVM-13 libcxx predates libc++ runtime bits that the nixpkgs `nix`
and the nixpkgs LLVM-21 toolchain need at load time:
  - <filesystem> sources shipped but unbuilt (0 std::filesystem symbols;
    libnixutil needs 26); add them.
  - std::pmr did not exist at all (only std::experimental::pmr; libc++ gained
    std::pmr in LLVM 16). Add a self-contained std::pmr: memory_resource +
    get_default_resource, and monotonic_buffer_resource ported from LLVM-17
    libcxx (matches the macOS-14 ABI nix was built against; libnixexpr
    constructs one via the inline ctor and needs its vtable + exact layout).
  - __libcpp_verbose_abort (the single verbose-termination handler libc++
    gained in LLVM 14) was absent, so the nixpkgs LLVM-21 clang/libLLVM failed
    to load under Darling (dyld "Symbol not found:
    __ZNSt3__122__libcpp_verbose_abortEPKcz") on every compile -- the last gap
    stopping guest `nix build` from compiling anything. Verified with llvm-nm to
    be the only genuine libc++ symbol the whole clang closure was missing. Add
    the standard stderr+abort() implementation (src/verbose_abort_std.cpp).

All the additions are forced to default visibility (libcxx builds
-fvisibility=hidden); the C++17 ones are compiled -std=c++17. The rest of
libc++ is C++11.

